# R session artifacts
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rapp.history
.Rproj.user/
*.Rproj

# profiler output
*.Rprof
prof_*.out

# Generated pipeline output - regenerate with run_pipeline.R.
# Not tracked: these are derived from the tracked sources, and git history
# now provides the regression baseline they used to serve as (check out an
# older commit and re-run to reproduce any previous output).
script_out.txt
script_out2.txt
scratch_full_out.qvs
formatexample_after.txt
script_qvs_out.txt

# benchmark / profiling scratch
chunk_timings.rds

# Claude Code settings that are local to this machine
.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-machine qlik-cli location and probe output. The path differs on every VM,
# so it is never tracked - qlik_cli_path.txt.example IS tracked as the template.
qlik_cli_path.txt
qlik_probe_out/

# Generated migration reports - regenerate with render_report.R.
report_app*.html
*-report.html

# Repo tidy-up (Adam 2026-08-21): this is a solo-dev repo, git is used purely
# as a delivery mechanism to get scripts onto VMs that never commit or push.
# Dev/test-only files stay on disk and stay usable here - they are just no
# longer tracked, so a VM operator browsing GitHub isn't wading through them.
# [Grant Managing Region].txt stays TRACKED on purpose - kept version
# controlled and available for VM-side troubleshooting even though unlikely
# to be needed.

# Example report output.
report_mock.html

# Example app folders.
app-unbuilt/
app2-unbuilt/

# Dev-only pipeline gate - never run on a VM, only before a push here.
# Bare name (no leading /) matches at any depth, so this still covers
# verify.R now that it lives at styling/verify.R (2026-08-21 reorg).
verify.R

# docs/ HAS ITS OWN GIT REPO (2026-08-24), and is ignored here on purpose.
#
# The working notes need history - DESIGN.md is 1778 lines and compacting a
# closed section is only safe if the prose can be diffed back. They do not need
# publishing: a VM operator downloads scripts and has no use for them. Git
# cannot track a file locally and withhold it from a push, so the two needs
# split into two repos. docs/ has NO REMOTE and must never be given one.
#
# Consequence to remember: `git status` here will never show a doc edit. Commit
# doc changes inside docs/ (cd docs && git commit), in the same session.
docs/

# 2026-08-21 folder reorg: console_ui.R writes results here, regenerated from
# the input app each run. The placeholder note IS tracked (explicit name, not
# matched by the wildcards) so the folder exists and explains itself on a
# fresh clone.
outputs/*
!outputs/RESULTS_LAND_HERE.txt

# input-apps/ has no generated content to ignore - only its placeholder note
# is tracked; whatever a user drops in there is theirs to manage, not ignored
# by this repo (they know what they put there).

# Dev fixtures: untracked 2026-08-24. They are inputs for verify.R, which is
# itself a dev-only gate that never runs on a VM - so a VM operator has no use
# for them, and they were the largest thing the repo carried for nobody.
fixtures/

# CLAUDE.md must sit at the repo root - the harness loads ./CLAUDE.md by path,
# so it cannot live in docs/ with the other working notes. It is ignored here
# for the same reason they are: it is session rules for the development
# machine, of no use to a VM operator, and not for publishing.
CLAUDE.md

# Crunch outputs that are pure derived data, regenerated by every run of
# build_retarget_map.R. The MAP itself stays tracked: DESIGN §6.6 wants it
# hand-editable and reviewable, and rp_merge() protects those edits.
retargeting/retarget_columns.csv
retargeting/retarget_payloads.json

# Generated by analysis/csv_viewer.R next to whatever csv it was pointed at.
*-view.html
